From: Seyoon Ragavan <complexzetaprime@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:44:59 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Encoding: renaming a machine's states preserves its
 computations, once; the coding steps cite it

- Turing.FinTM.computesInTime_relabelState: renaming a bundled machine's states along an
  equivalence gives a machine with the same computations.
- Turing.FinTM.stateEquivFin: a bundled machine's states as Fin (|State| - 1 + 1).
- exists_codeTM_spaceUsed's time clause, FinTM.toCodeTM, toCodeTM_computesInTime_iff and
  Codes2Tape's exists_code2TM use them, instead of each repeating the renaming argument.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
